@url = http://localhost:3000

### ---------- INSCRIPTION ----------

### Inscription → 201, avec id, username et email (PAS de mot de passe)
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alex@example.com", "username": "alex", "password": "Password123" }

### Mêmes données une 2e fois → 409
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alex@example.com", "username": "alex", "password": "Password123" }

### Même email, autre pseudo → 409
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alex@example.com", "username": "alexbis", "password": "Password123" }

### Email invalide → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alex-example.com", "username": "alex2", "password": "Password123" }

### Pseudo avec caractères spéciaux → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a2@example.com", "username": "al!ex", "password": "Password123" }

### Pseudo trop court (moins de 3) → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a3@example.com", "username": "al", "password": "Password123" }

### Pseudo trop long (plus de 20) → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a3b@example.com", "username": "unpseudobeaucouptroplong", "password": "Password123" }

### Mot de passe sans majuscule → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a4@example.com", "username": "alex4", "password": "password123" }

### Mot de passe trop court → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "a5@example.com", "username": "alex5", "password": "Pass12" }

### Body vide → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### ---------- CONNEXION ----------

### Connexion → 200 avec le token
# @name login
POST {{url}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alex@example.com", "password": "Password123" }

### Mauvais mot de passe (mauvaise casse) → 401 "Email ou mot de passe incorrect"
POST {{url}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alex@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### Email inexistant → 401, EXACTEMENT le même message
POST {{url}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "personne@example.com", "password": "Password123" }

### Body vide → 400
POST {{url}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### ---------- DÉCONNEXION ----------

### Déconnexion → 200 (le token vient de la requête "login" ci-dessus)
POST {{url}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Déconnexion sans token → 401
POST {{url}}/auth/logout

### Déconnexion avec un faux token → 401
POST {{url}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi